# ─── SPA Fallback for Netlify ────────────────────────────
# When someone visits qazan.fi/menu directly, Netlify's server
# looks for a file called /menu. There is no such file — it's
# a React route. Without this rule, you get a 404.
#
# This rule says: "For ANY path that doesn't match a real file,
# serve index.html instead (with a 200 status, not a redirect)."
# Then React Router takes over and renders the correct page.
#
# The 200 (not 301/302) is important — it means "serve this file
# AS IF it was the requested URL" rather than redirecting.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

/*    /index.html   200
